#: src/project/changelog.md:7
msgid ""
"Report duplicate `import` definitions as an error rather than silently "
"keeping the last one. `import a.b` followed by `import c.b` now reports "
"`duplicate declarations of b`, matching `let` and `type`; use `import d = c."
"b` to bring in both. The same applies to a multi-file project, where `import "
"a.b` previously discarded a sibling `b.prql`. This is a small breaking "
"change — programs that relied on the last declaration winning now fail to "
"compile. (@prql-bot, #6150)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/changelog.md:14
msgid ""
"Move all standard types into a dedicated `std.types` submodule in order to "
"disambiguate between `type text` - `module text` and `type date` - `module "
"date`. (@kgutwin, #6155)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project/changelog.md:17
msgid ""
"_Breaking_: The compile target `sql.glaredb` has been removed, since it was "
"never tested after GlareDB's full rewrite, and GlareDB seems to be no longer "
"maintained. (@eitsupi, #6172)"
msgstr ""

